\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 1.0\tab purpose\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 The purpose of this procedure is to outline procedure for ensuring competency of ESPAK personnel involved in the sampling, testing & monitoring, reporting, and related activities.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 2.0\tab SCOPE\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 The Procedure applies to all laboratory personnel working in ESPAK. \par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 3.0\tab RESPONSIBILITY\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 3.1.\tab Chief Analyst/ Management Representative (MR) is responsible to;\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb120\qj\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Ensure implementation of the procedure related to his/her part.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Develop and get approved the competence requirements for specific tasks.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Assist in the selection of personnel for induction.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Ensure that record of trainings is maintained.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Ensures personnel receive training and demonstrate competence.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Forward training proposals developed in accordance with Training Need Assessments. \par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Ensure work is only assigned to competent personnel.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 3.2.\tab Quality Assurance Manager is responsible to;\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb120\qj\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Review competence requirements for specific activities.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Identify training needs resulting from non-conforming work and monitoring activities.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Decide on the authorization of lab personnel, and periodically update, with the help of Management System Coordinator, Lab Authorization Permits.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Make plans for, and implement internal competency checks.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 3.3.\tab General Manager is responsible to\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb120\qj\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Approve the competence requirements of personnel.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Approving the selection and appointment of personnel.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Deputing the supervisors of personnel, and\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Other functions ancillary to these functions.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s1\fi-907\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning28\b\caps 4.0\tab PROCEDURE\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\kerning0\b0\caps0 4.1.\tab Determination of Competence Requirements (Eligibility Criteria)\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.1.1.\tab Chief Chemist/Management Representative proposes competence requirements for specific position or job in any of the following situations.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li900\sb120\qj\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Directions received from higher management for alteration in scope of laboratory work, requiring new slots to be developed, or re-defining scope of work of existing slots.\par

\pard\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb120\qj\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Re-organization of laboratory structure or management system necessitating change in competence requirements.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Change in applicable requirements of regulatory authorities or accreditation bodies.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Change or revision of methods used in performing laboratory functions.\par
\f3\'d8\tab\f1 Any other situation requiring defining or re-defining competency requirements.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.1.2.\tab Competence requirements (Eligibility Criteria) are reviewed by Quality Assurance Manager and Human Resource Manager jointly and sent to General Manager for approval.\par
4.1.3.\tab After approval from General Manager, hiring or any further training of existing staff may begin.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.2.\tab Selection of Personnel\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.2.1.\tab When there is a vacancy in ESPAK, a Personnel Requisition form is filled out by the supervisor and forwarded to HR manager.\par
4.2.2.\tab HR manager gets the approval from General Manager and advertises the post.\par
4.2.3.\tab After job application receiving process is complete, HR manager, in consultation with supervisor, sorts out and shortlists the applicants according to competence requirements.\par
4.2.4.\tab Short listed candidates are interviewed by HR manager accompanied by a senior person having expertise.\par
4.2.5.\tab Applicants short listed by interview process are forwarded to General Manger for re-interview.\par
4.2.6.\tab Final Selection is done by General Manger and HR manager appoints the selected persons.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\qj\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.3.\tab Training of Personnel\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.3.1.\tab After new selection or implementation of new procedures or revision of existing procedures, supervisor or any senior person noting the deficiency writes a training need assessment form.\par
4.3.2.\tab The form is handed over to Management system coordinator who gets approval from General manger on the recommendation of QA manager.\par
4.3.3.\tab After approval and as directed by General Manger, training is executed filling out training record forms and evaluations. All these activities are coordinated by Management System Coordinator.\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.4.\tab Supervision of Personnel\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.4.1.\tab All the personnel are supervised by a supervisor, duly authorized by General Manager. If no such authorization is present, it will be deemed that the personnel will be supervised by his immediate senior in hierarchy.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\tx2280\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.5.\tab Authorization of Personnel\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.5.1.\tab Supervisor is to recommend the authorization of all the personnel after he is satisfied that the personnel proposed for authorization has met all competence requirements.\par
4.5.2.\tab After successful training and competency assessment, the incumbent or newly trained personnel may be authorized by QA Manger for specific assignments.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj\par

\pard\keepn\nowidctlpar\s2\fi-900\sb120\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.6.\tab Monitoring Competence of Personnel\par

\pard\keep\keepn\widctlpar\s3\fi-810\li810\sb200\sl26\slmult0\qj 4.6.1.\tab QA Manger chalks out annual competency monitoring plan for all authorized personnel.\par
4.6.2.\tab Competency checks may be prepared by blind samples, known competency samples, or jobs or any other methods suitable for the competency monitoring to be executed.\par
4.6.3.\tab Record of competency monitoring so executed is kept by QA manager.\par
4.6.4.\tab If there is any discrepancy or competency check fails, corrective action is initiated.\par

